/-!
# Real time, imaginary time, stochastic sampling, physical diffusion, and open return are distinct

**[proved-derived]** Physlib's finite self-adjoint Hamiltonian supplies a unitary real-time group.
The imaginary-time exponential is a separate nonunitary semigroup.  The standing Holonics Markov
kernel preserves probability mass, while the standing port-resolved physical passage telescopes
stored quantity, incoming current, and addressed boundary return.  Open-system transport has its own
typed channel carrier.

The types deliberately provide no coercion among these passages.  Wick rotation, stochastic
representation, hydrodynamic limits, and analytic continuation remain separate bridge obligations.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace Soma.Holonics.Computation.HolonicEvolutionKinds

open scoped BigOperators
open Soma.Holonics.Computation.HolonicDiffusionCharts
